      "description": "Careers | 香港珠海學院 | Hong Kong Chu Hai College Current Students | Staff | Alumni Donation Library 繁體 简体 About Us About the College Vision & Missions Governance Management Structure President's Message Campus & Facilities Map & Directions Administrative College Videos College Publications Admissions About the Admissions Undergraduate Postgraduate Higher Diploma Academics Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences Faculty of Business Faculty of Science and Engineering Ng Teng Fong · Sino Group Belt and Road Research Institute Campus Life HOME Careers Careers Research / Project Positions Administrative Positions Academic Positions Management Positions Ng Teng Fong․ Sino Group Belt and Road Research Institute Research Fellow/Research Associate (3 headcounts; full-time for 9 months, renewable subject to performance and funding availability) Project Ref. No.: CHC/RMGS/19/001(Project title: Belt and Road Studies - Development of Economy, Industries and Trade in Belt and Road Countries) Responsibilities · Assist project leader on research projects on “Belt and Road Studies - Development of Economy, Industries and Trade in Belt and Road Countries”; · Assist in liaising and communication with external stakeholders; · Assist in organizing research activities including conferences and seminars; and · Assist in data collection, data analysis, etc.. Requirements: · A doctoral degree or equivalent qualification on Belt and Road Studies; · At least 5 years post-qualification or relevant research experiences ; · Have a good command of both written and spoken English and if possible fluent speaking Mandarin; · Have a strong organizational and communication skills. Closing Date: Consideration of applications will continue until the position is filled. Application Applicants are invited to send their detailed curriculum vitae, including current and expected salary, and direct any enquiries to the Human Resources Office, Hong Kong Chu Hai College [E-mail: recruitment@chuhai.edu.hk], quoting the position being applied for and the reference number. Recruitment will continue until the position is filled. Candidature may be obtained by nominations. The College reserves the right to make an appointment by invitation or not to fill this post. About Us Admissions Academics Library Current Students Staff Alumni Copyright © Hong Kong Chu Hai College. All rights reserved. | Address: 80 Castle Peak Road, Castle Peak Bay, Tuen Mun, N.T. Hong Kong. | Tel: (852) 2972 7200 | Fax: (852) 2972 7367 | Email: info@chuhai.edu.hk"
