      "title": "香港珠海學院 | Hong Kong Chu Hai College",
      "description": "Careers | 香港珠海學院 | Hong Kong Chu Hai College Current Students | Staff | Alumni Donation Library 繁體 简体 About Us About the College Vision & Missions Governance Management Structure President's Message Campus & Facilities Map & Directions Administrative College Videos College Publications Admissions About the Admissions Undergraduate Postgraduate Higher Diploma Academics Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences Faculty of Business Faculty of Science and Engineering Ng Teng Fong · Sino Group Belt and Road Research Institute Campus Life HOME Careers Careers Research / Project Positions Administrative Positions Academic Positions Management Positions Kong Mou Sum Library Librarian 圖書館館長 (Ref:LIB/LIB/LA/1) Librarian Hong Kong Chu Hai College Limited Hong Kong Chu Hai College(香港珠海學院) is established and registered as an Approved Post-Secondary College under the Post-Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap 320).  It has provided more than 70 years of quality education and excellence to the Hong Kong community and remains committed to enhancing the educational opportunities for young people in Hong Kong. Its purpose and vision are to nurture future leaders, strengthen the competitiveness of Hong Kong, and help bring about a stable, prosperous and harmonious society in a knowledge-based economic environment. To know more about us, you are welcome to visit www.chuhai.edu.hk Human Resources Office Email: recruitment@chuhai.edu.hk Key Responsibilities Ensure Library’s resources and services are able to meet learning, teaching and research needs Support collection development of printed and online resources Develop close partnership with publishers and resources providers and keep abreast of the latest trends in electronic resources including online books and journals Promote library’s services and resources via various channels and engage with the academic and student communities to evaluate users’ needs Advise and support faculties on dissemination and preservation of research output, enhance research impact, and use bibliographical citation management tools Implement College’s policies in acquiring books, journals, periodicals and e-materials Supervise paraprofessional staff in circulation, cataloging, classification and organization of learning resource materials to assure maximum accessibility and usefulness Carry out such other duties as may be assigned by the Registrar Skills and Qualifications: A recognized university degree and professional qualification in librarianship (MLS or equivalent) with 5 years of post-qualification experience and supervisory responsibilities Good planning and organizational skills Ability to work independently as well as cooperatively and collegially with colleagues Excellent interpersonal and communication skills in English and Chinese Demonstrable professionalism with strong motivation, innovation, flexibility and commitment Application: Interested parties please send full resume with salary expectation and availability by sending email to: recruitment@chuhai.edu.hk Personal data provided by job applicants will be kept strictly confidential and used for employment related purpose. About Us Admissions Academics Library Current Students Staff Alumni Copyright © Hong Kong Chu Hai College. All rights reserved. | Address: 80 Castle Peak Road, Castle Peak Bay, Tuen Mun, N.T. Hong Kong. | Tel: (852) 2972 7200 | Fax: (852) 2972 7367 | Email: info@chuhai.edu.hk"
